      "stageRecord": "Mari is a nominative proper-name NP. Uut ajalehte is an NP whose noun is modified by an AP adjoined to N′; Estonian does not require an overt article here, so no determiner projection is stipulated. First, the AP establishes an intersective modifier relation with the nominal projection: the newspaper is new. Second, uut agrees with ajalehte in singular number and partitive case. Finally, the lexical forms establish the morphological specifications: Mari is nominative singular, uut and ajalehte are partitive singular, and loeb is the present indicative active third-person singular form of lugema. The verb is entered as the whole inflected word loeb; this analysis does not split its surface spelling into separate terminals. These objects are not yet combined into a clause, and the object's morphological partitive has not yet received its syntactic licensing.",
