      "stageRecord": "The verb first combines with uut ajalehte as its NP complement, establishing the verb's internal-argument selection and assigning that NP the Theme role. The nominal partitive is then licensed as the object case of this reading predicate: the sentence presents newspaper-reading without asserting a bounded, completed reading of the entire newspaper. Partitive case does not itself decide between an ongoing and a habitual interpretation, so those interpretations do not require separate syntactic analyses. Mari is subsequently merged in Spec-VP and receives the external Agent role. This adopts a VP-internal subject analysis: the position shown here is the subject's theta position, not its final surface position. The adjective remains inside the object NP and is not a secondary predicate.",
