      "stageRecord": "First, loeb raises from the previously represented V position and adjoins to I. A silent V trace replaces it inside V′, while the overt verb retains its lexical spelling and token association in the resulting complex I head. This head movement establishes the finite verb's relation to I without introducing a second pronounced copy. Second, Mari raises from the previously represented Spec-VP position to Spec-IP, leaving a silent NP trace in its theta position. This A-movement satisfies I's subject requirement. Third, the Spec-IP relation licenses Mari's nominative case and establishes third-person singular subject–verb agreement. The subject receives no additional theta role in Spec-IP; its chain retains the Agent role assigned in Spec-VP. The verb's trace preserves the predicate's relation to its object and its previously established partitive-case licensing.",
